spec:
  grid: 12-17 rows x 14-19 cols, black background
  colors: exactly 2 distinct non-black foreground colors
  anchor:
    shape: solid rectangle, 2-8 rows x 5-7 cols (area 10-49)
  moving_object:
    body: solid rectangle, 3-6 rows x 3-8 cols (area 9-48); must be the UNIQUE largest solid rectangle within the moving-color mask
    stem: straight 1-cell-wide contiguous segment, length 3-5, extending from one edge of body toward anchor
    connectivity: body + stem form a single 4-connected component
    stem_attachment: stem row/col lies within anchor's perpendicular span
  spatial:
    slide_direction: any of up/down/left/right; stem points from body toward anchor
    gap: stem end is exactly adjacent to anchor (0-cell gap); stem bridges body to anchor
    body_perpendicular_span: body extent along axis perpendicular to slide overlaps anchor by >= body's perpendicular extent [observed]
  margins: all foreground >=1 cell from grid border [observed]
  output:
    erase entire moving-color object (body + stem)
    place body rectangle adjacent to anchor, translated by stem_length in stem direction
    both objects are solid rectangles in output, touching along one edge

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size (12-17 x 14-19), two distinct non-black colors.
    2. Build the OUTPUT state first -- place anchor rectangle and body rectangle adjacent (sharing an edge), both on background, with >=1 margin from borders.
    3. Choose which side of the anchor the body touches; that determines slide direction.
    4. Pick stem_length (3-5). Choose a single row/col within the body's edge facing the anchor for the stem line.
    5. Derive INPUT by moving body away from anchor by stem_length cells in the opposite direction, then drawing the 1-cell-wide stem connecting the body's original edge to its new position.
    6. Verify: body+stem fit in grid with margin >=1, body is unique largest solid rect, stem end is adjacent to anchor, no overlap between objects.
